Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/net/SSLCertificateSocketFactory.java at android-15.0.0_r1
(Apache-2.0): getHttpSocketFactory is left out.

Why: the method returns org.apache.http.conn.ssl.SSLSocketFactory, a legacy Apache HTTP type that framework.jar does not
hold (org.apache.http is a named limit in fixtures/corpus/api-limits.txt), and it has been deprecated since API 22. The
rest of the class is unchanged.

